# Local development only. `wrangler dev` reads this file; `wrangler deploy` never
# uploads it, which is the whole safety argument for the variable below.
#
# Committed on purpose, for the same reason `localConnectionString` in
# wrangler.toml is: a dev setup that needs a secret before it will start is a dev
# setup people work around. There is nothing secret here — the value is a made-up
# owner id, the same shape Supabase Auth's `sub` has in production.
#
# With this set, every authenticated route accepts any bearer token and attributes
# the work to this owner. Without it, the real JWT path runs and refuses
# everything until SUPABASE_URL is configured. See `devVerifier` in src/auth.ts.
DEV_OWNER_ID = "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001"
